# The WeDoBooks SDK - which runs the ebook reader and the audiobook player -
# is published to WeDoBooks' own registry, not to npm. Colibrio, the reading
# framework underneath it, is mirrored there too.
#
# This has to live at the workspace root rather than next to the package that
# uses it: pnpm reads .npmrc from the directory it is invoked in, and both CI
# and the Lagoon images install the whole workspace from here.
#
# Only the scope mapping belongs in this file. The token is a credential and
# stays out of the repository: `task init:pnpm` reads WEDOBOOKS_NPM_TOKEN from
# the central .env and hands it to pnpm as an environment config key. For a
# bare `pnpm install` run outside Task, put it in the user-level npm config
# once instead:
#
#     pnpm config set "//npm.pkg.wedobooks.io/:_authToken" "$WEDOBOOKS_NPM_TOKEN"
#
# Do not reference the variable from this file as ${WEDOBOOKS_NPM_TOKEN}.
# pnpm discards an .npmrc it cannot fully expand, so wherever the variable is
# unset the scope mappings below would silently disappear too.
#
# See packages/wedobooks/README.md.
@wedobooks:registry=https://npm.pkg.wedobooks.io
@colibrio:registry=https://npm.pkg.wedobooks.io
